# Antifragility Source Summary

Antifragility is presented as a universal mental model for understanding how complex systems, organisms, and strategies benefit from disorder, volatility, and stressors. The source is a metadata stub pointing to Nassim Nicholas Taleb's *Antifragile* as the authoritative reference. Key principles include convexity, optionality, the fragility-antifragility spectrum, skin in the game, and barbell strategy. This model connects to existing Taleb-related entries including [[skin-in-the-game---nassim-nicholas-taleb]] and [[the-black-swan---nassim-nicholas-taleb]].